<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Chakan</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1542 CE (approx.) · capital T'ho</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya province of north-western Yucatán around T'ho, on whose ruins the Spanish founded the city of Mérida in 1542.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Chakan was one of the provinces formed after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441. It covered the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tho">T'ho</a> (Ichcaansihó), an old centre with large pyramids, in the north-west of the peninsula.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Unlike the more centralised provinces, Chakan appears to have had no single overlord; its towns were governed by batabs of several lineages, including the Canché, who cooperated loosely. Its people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and kept bees, and the coastal area produced salt. It is known chiefly from Spanish colonial records.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1542 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo-the-younger">Francisco de Montejo the Younger</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merida-yucatan">Mérida</a> on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tho">T'ho</a>, using its stones for the new buildings, and Chakan became the core of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1441 CE – 1542 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.38%;width:2.01%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1542 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>T'ho</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chakán</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=chakan" aria-label="Chakan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1956 1296 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chakan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2276 1552h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2276 1552h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mexico. <a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=chakan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
